## Coda

One Ground.

Many real dependent forms.

One Light.

Many real reflections.

Many trajectories.

Many centers of experience.

Their distinction is real.

Their suffering is real.

Their joy is real.

Their being is God’s.

Pride says:

I am the Ground.

Ignorance says:

I am separate.

Despair says:

The gift should never have been given.

Humility says:

I receive.

Love says:

Your life is good also.

The Good says:

No one is finally expendable.

Freedom says:

I answer.

Responsibility says:

The Good is mine to affirm.

Authorship says:

What I did is mine.

Culpability says:

I answer according to the freedom and sight I possess.

Consequence says:

What I do becomes part of what follows.

Grace says:

I know the whole truth, and I will not leave you.

Courage says:

Nevertheless, life.

Communion says:

Not separate.

And Life says:

Yes.

The Ground is immutable.

The forms change.

The trajectories continue.

Grace seeks redemption.

Freedom answers.

The dance has no known first step and no known last.

The dance is good.

The Ground is not elsewhere. The work is here: in the truth we tell, the harm we refuse, the suffering we relieve, and the love we give.

Look and see.

And beneath every word, every body, every birth, every death, every transformation, every creature, every joy, every wound, every refusal, every consequence, every act of grace, every reflection, every Yes, and every return:

There is only God.
